@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-cancellation-refund-policy-full-48h-or-more-before-start-half-before-start-none-after
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancellation refund policy: full 48h or more before start, half before start, none after"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Customers ask to cancel bookings. The request defines `cancel(bookingId, at)` returning
+`{ bookingId, refund }`, but not how much is refunded. This is a money rule, so it needs approval
+before it is implemented.
+
+## Decision
+
+Proposed policy (integer euro cents, relative to the booking's start; `at` is an ISO-8601 instant):
+
+- `at` 48 hours or more before the start: refund the full total.
+- `at` less than 48 hours before the start: refund half the total, rounded to the nearest cent.
+- `at` at or after the start: refund 0; the booking is still cancelled.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: its period is free for new bookings.
+- A booking can be cancelled once; an unknown id or an already cancelled booking throws.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Thresholds and percentages are constants, easy to change if the school wants another policy.
